{{Elections in Michigan}}

The '''1990 United States Senate election in Michigan''' was held on November 6, 1990. Incumbent [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic]] U.S. Senator [[Carl Levin]] won re-election to a third term against future [[Michigan attorney general]] [[Bill Schuette]], who was still serving as Michigan's 10th district representative.

== Candidates ==

===Democratic ===
* [[Carl Levin]], incumbent U.S. Senator

===Republican ===
* [[Clark Durant]], attorney and founder of Cornerstone Schools<ref>{{cite news | last = Eggert | first = David | title = Republican Clark Durant loses bid for U.S. Senate 22 years after 1st attempt | url = https://www.mlive.com/politics/index.ssf/2012/08/clark_durant_michigan_senate.html | access-date = August 8, 2012 | newspaper = mlive | date = August 7, 2012}}</ref>
* [[Bill Schuette]], U.S. representative

===Workers World ===
* Susan Farquhar

